      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "1. What is the syntax of the for loop, and what are its parts?",
          "bold": true,
          "italic": false,
          "underline": false,
          "mono": false
        }
      ],
      "align": "left",
      "indent": false
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "The statements to be repeated are kept inside a block of code, and the for loop has three parts inside its parentheses, separated by semicolons: (1) initialization, where the loop starts; (2) condition, until where it should go; and (3) increment or decrem",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "underline": false,
          "mono": false
        },
        {
          "text": "ent, how the value changes on every repetition. for is a reserved keyword in Java.",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "underline": false,
          "mono": false
        }
      ],
      "align": "left",
      "indent": false
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "text": "for (initialization; condition; increment/decrement) {\n    // statements to repeat\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "2. Write a program that prints \"StringStack\" five times using a for loop.",
          "bold": true,
          "italic": false,
          "underline": false,
          "mono": false
        }
      ],
      "align": "left",
      "indent": false
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Start from 1, ",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "underline": false,
          "mono": false
        },
        {
          "text": "go until 5, and increase by 1 each time. Instead of five copies of the statement, only one is written inside the loop block.",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "underline": false,
          "mono": false
        }
      ],
      "align": "left",
      "indent": false
    },
