    {
      "type": "code",
      "text": "Three things change: the loop starts from 10, the condition becomes i >= 1 (greater than or equal, because the value is decreasing), and the update becomes i-- (decrement) instead of i++.\npublic class Demo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        for (int i = 10; i >= 1; i--) {\n            System.out.println(i);\n        }\n    }\n}"
